{:adr-id "2607171200"
 :title "cloud-itonami-isic-0142 (raising of horses and other equines) equine-facility-operations-coordination actor"
 :status :accepted
 :date "2026-07-15"
 :deciders ["Jun Kawasaki (agent-executed, standing authorization)"]
 :related ["ADR-2607152100" "ADR-2607122200" "ADR-2607011000"]

 :context
 "ISIC Rev. 4 class 0142 (Raising of horses and other equines) had no cloud-itonami
  implementation; registry entry was :maturity :spec with a never-created
  gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-A0142 placeholder repo. Identity verified fresh from a clean
  clone of kotoba-lang/industry before any work began: {:id \"0142\" :name \"Raising of
  horses and other equines\"} matches the assigned scope exactly (a prior fleet
  incident mislabeled 0892/0144 against their actual registry names, so this check is
  mandatory). Racing/gambling activities are explicitly out of scope -- this actor
  covers raising/breeding operations coordination only."

 :scope-exclusions
 ["direct animal handling (stable operator's exclusive authority)"
  "veterinary treatment decisions (veterinarian/stable operator authority)"
  "breeding or culling decisions (economic and ethical authority remains human)"
  "racing or gambling activities (categorically out of scope, no corresponding op)"]

 :decision
 "Implement cloud-itonami-isic-0142 with Governor, Facts, Registry, Store, Advisor,
  Phase, Operation, Sim (mirrors cloud-itonami-isic-0141/cattleops and
  cloud-itonami-isic-0145/swineops module-for-module), namespace `equineops`:
  - Governor (Equine Facility Operations Governor): 5 hard checks
    (facility-not-registered, no-execution, treatment-or-breeding-culling-blocked,
    op-not-allowed, herd-count-invalid) + 3 escalation gates (always-escalate health
    concern, cost-threshold supply orders, low confidence < 0.7)
  - blocked-ops = #{:administer-treatment :order-breeding-culling-decision} --
    direct treatment administration AND breeding/culling decisions are both
    permanently blocked (adapted from cattle/swine's :order-slaughter, since horses
    are commonly raised for breeding/working/riding rather than slaughter)
  - Facts: supply categories with cost thresholds (feed/veterinary-supply 500,
    tack 1000), species (horse/donkey/mule), health-concern vocabulary
    (equine-influenza/colic/strangles/laminitis, purely descriptive -- never
    changes the always-escalate disposition)
  - Registry: independent pure predicates (cost-exceeds-threshold?,
    herd-count-non-positive?, confidence-below-floor?)
  - Store: Store protocol + MemStore (registered-facility lookup)
  - Advisor: Advisor protocol + MockAdvisor (4 ops)
  - Phase: 0->3 rollout gate
  - Operation: composes advisor -> governor -> phase-gate (langgraph-clj wiring
    deferred, matching 0141/0145's own stub)
  - Sim: demo runner with a working -main
  - Operations: log-herd-record, schedule-veterinary-visit,
    flag-animal-health-concern, order-supplies (closed allowlist, :effect :propose)
  - Tests: 31 tests / 96 assertions (facts, governor, phase, registry, store), all
    green -- includes an extra hard-violations-breeding-culling-blocked test beyond
    the 0141/0145 shape to independently verify the equine-specific blocked op
  - All .cljc (portable, no JVM interop), AGPL-3.0-or-later
  - README/docs describe the real API (equineops.operation run-operation/build,
    :commit/:escalate/:hold dispositions)"

 :consequences
 {:positive
  ["Equine-raising (0142) now genuinely implemented and fully tested"
   "Scope boundaries (animal handling, treatment, breeding/culling, racing/gambling)
    hardcoded in governor checks and closed op-allowlist, not just asserted in prose"
   "Animal-welfare escalation (flag-animal-health-concern always human) is a core
    design invariant"
   "Portable .cljc, zero JVM-only constructs, clj-kondo 0 errors / 0 warnings"]
  :negative
  ["Real persistent store (Datomic/kotoba-server) is a follow-up (in-memory for now)"
   "langgraph-clj StateGraph wiring (real interrupt-before/checkpoint resume) is
    deferred scaffolding, matching 0141/0145's own stub status"]}

